# House style for NEW files only. Not auto-discovered, on purpose.
#
# clang-format walks up from a source file looking for a file literally named
# `.clang-format`, so anything with that name in the repo root is applied by
# Visual Studio and by the VS Code C/C++ extension as you type. The root config
# is therefore a deliberate no-op (see `.clang-format`), and this file - which
# no tool discovers - holds the style itself.
#
# Use it explicitly, and only on a file you have just created:
#
#     clang-format --style=file:tools/house-style.clang-format -i <newfile>
#
# Never run it over an existing file. Measured 31 Aug 2026 with clang-format
# 20.1.8 and re-measured 1 Sep 2026: even with the settings below tuned toward
# the house style, 92 of 123 C++ files and 1,961 sites still differ. The tree's
# formatting is hand-tuned per site - aligned `case` returns, line breaks chosen
# for readability, grouped initialiser lists - and a formatter destroys that
# information rather than normalising it. See
# `.claude/rules/cpp-conventions.md` for the rule.
#
# Settings below the base style were chosen by measuring the tree, not by
# preference: BreakBeforeBinaryOperators and AlignAfterOpenBracket each cut
# divergence materially (2,885 -> 2,012 sites together). Two were tried and
# rejected: SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 2 made 30 more files diverge, because
# the tree uses one space; AlignConsecutiveShortCaseStatements looked like it
# would rescue the aligned `case` returns and moved only 16 of 1,961 sites.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 100
BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Inline
SortIncludes: CaseInsensitive
PointerAlignment: Left
ReferenceAlignment: Left

# Operators lead the continuation line: `... \n || cond` not `... || \n cond`.
BreakBeforeBinaryOperators: NonAssignment
# Continuation indents by one level rather than aligning to the open bracket.
AlignAfterOpenBracket: DontAlign
# `case LogLevel::Info: return "INFO";` stays on one line.
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
